  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 243 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nTemperatures peak on Friday with good warm air advection ahead of \nthe approaching trough. Afternoon high temperatures in the low to \nmid 60s are expected across the state. Once again expect to see\nbreezy conditions as the pressure gradient tightens with the \napproaching system. By Saturday this wraps up into a more robust\nlow that moves across the upper midwest while a southern stream\nvort max within the base of the trough scoots across the \nplains. The trailing cold front between the two streams reaches \nwestern Iowa Saturday and passes across the state overnight. \nTemperatures swing from the 60s on Saturday to the 40s on \nSunday. Those cooler temperatures last through at least early \nnext week.\n\nAlong with the temperature swing Saturday and Sunday comes the \nnext chance for widespread precipitation across the state. A \nwidespread quarter to half inch of rain is possible. A ribbon of\ninstability, about 50-200 J/kg of MLCAPE, may also result in \nthunderstorms. At this time modest instability will prevent any\nsevere potential.",
